  "verbalization": "Ammonium Lactate is associated with Atopic Eczema through a series of indications, which in turn link to Dermatitis, Atopic. This suggests that Ammonium Lactate may exert a therapeutic effect on Atopic Eczema, potentially through mechanisms that are shared with other treatments like Crisaborole, Pimecrolimus, and Dupilumab. These medications are all used to manage atopic dermatitis, indicating a possible overlap in their biological pathways. The high scores in the evidence suggest that the relationship between Ammonium Lactate and Atopic Eczema is robust, with the indication chain pointing to Dermatitis, Atopic as a downstream effect. The integration of these pathways implies that Ammonium Lactate may act through a mechanism that is similarly effective in treating atopic dermatitis, possibly by modulating immune responses or inflammatory pathways. The evidence supports a role for Ammonium Lactate in the management of atopic dermatitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
